[0.000, "o", "  \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending_approval\\\",\\r\\n\"]\r\n../demo/e2e-local.cast:174:[0.016, \"o\", \"\\r\\n\\u001b[1;32m[OK]\\u001b[0m \\u001b[1;36mset_label (gated)\\u001b[0m\\r\\n   \\u001b[0;90mStamp a fleet label through the same propose/approve gate - labels drive Placements, so they are write-gated too.\\u001b[0m\\r\\n   \\u001b[0;90m$ tool: apply_cluster_action(set_label)\\u001b[0m\\r\\n     {\\r\\n       \\\"cluster\\\": \\\"cluster1\\\",\\r\\n       \\\"action\\\": \\\"set_label\\\",\\r\\n       \\\"status\\\": \\\"applied\\\"\\r\\n     }\\r\\n\"]\r\n../demo/e2e-local.cast:191:[0.000, \"o\", \"\\r\\n\\u001b[1;32m[OK]\\u001b[0m \\u001b[1;36mprompt: why_not_scheduled\\u001b[0m\\r\\n   \\u001b[0;90mA ready-made, safety-first runbook an agent can start from.\\u001b[0m\\r\\n   \\u001b[0;90m$ mcp prompt: why_not_scheduled\\u001b[0m\\r\\n     Explain why cluster 'cluster1' was or was not selected by Placement 'demo-all' in namespace 'default'. Use only reads:\\r\\n     \\r\\n     1. get_placement_decision('demo-all', 'default') for the clusters actually chosen.\\r\\n     2. list_placements to read th"]
[0.000, "o", "e Placement's clusterSets and selection intent.\\r\\n     3. get_cluster('cluster1') for its labels, ClusterClaims, and taints.\\r\\n\"]\r\n../demo/e2e-local.cast:192:[0.000, \"o\", \"     4. list_cluster_set_bindings to confirm the Placement's namespace is bound to the ClusterSet the cluster belongs to.\\r\\n     5. list_addon_placement_scores('cluster1') if the Placement uses AddOn prioritizers.\\r\\n\"]\r\n../demo/e2e-local.cast:210:[0.000, \"o\", \"     2. Identify the Placement it targets, then call get_placement_decision to list the clusters in scope.\\r\\n     3. For any cluster that looks stuck, call get_manifestwork(cluster, <name>) to read the per-resource conditions and status feedback and find what is blocking Apply/Available.\\r\\n     4. Summarize progress across the fleet and name the specific clusters and resources that are not yet healthy, with evidence.\\r\\n\"]\r\n../demo/connect-codex.cast:13:[0.000, \"o\", \"  (codex reads examples/codex-config.toml - see examples/README.md)\\r\\n\\r\\n\\u001b[1;36m# 3b. fixtures: a cluster-"]
[0.000, "o", "set binding, a Placement, and the target namespace\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\"]\r\n../demo/connect-codex.cast:14:[0.002, \"o\", \"  placement demo-all + namespace shop ready\\r\\n\"]\r\n../demo/connect-codex.cast:46:[0.000, \"o\", \"gistration, policy, and `get_cluster_info` are all\\r\\ndocs/tools.md:28:  concurrently across every cluster (`OCM_MCP_FANOUT_WORKERS`, default 8); a cluster\\r\\ndocs/tools.md:49:`OCM_MCP_READ_ONLY=1` makes every **propose** and **apply** tool refuse before doing\\r\\ndocs/tools.md:63:| `get_cluster` | read | `cluster` | `ManagedCluster` (acceptance, taints, version, capacity, claims) |\\r\\ndocs/tools.md:74:| `get_fleet_health` | read | `clusters?` | whole-fleet hub conditions + concurrent spoke pods/deployments (`OCM_MCP_FANOUT_WORKERS`); broken spokes are an `error` entry, not a failed call |\\r\\ndocs/tools.md:84:| `list_addon_placement_scores` | read | `cluster` | `AddOnPlacementScore` v1alpha1 |\\r\\ndocs/tools.md:100:## addons\\r\\ndocs/tools.md:104:| `list_cluster_management_addons` | read | - | `ClusterManageme"]
[0.000, "o", "ntAddOn` v1alpha1 + install strategy |\\r\\ndocs/tools.md:105:| `get_addon_health` | read | - | `ManagedClusterAddOn` v1alpha1 Available/Degraded per cluster |\\r\\ndocs/tools.md:106:| `list_addons_for_cluster` | read | `cluster\"]\r\n../demo/connect-codex.cast:70:[0.000, \"o\", \"\\r\\n<details>\\r\\n<summary><b>inventory</b> - who is in the fleet</summary>\\r\\n\\r\\n- **`list_clusters`** *(read)* - all managed clusters with availability, version, labels, capacity.\\r\\n- **`get_cluster`** *(read)* - full view of one cluster.\\r\\n  - `cluster` (string) - managed cluster name.\\r\\n- **`list_cluster_sets`** *(read)* - ManagedClusterSets with selector type and member clusters.\\r\\n- **`list_cluster_set_bindings`** *(read)* - which ClusterSets a namespace's Placements may target.\\r\\n  - `namespace` (string, optional) - limit to one namespace; empty lists all.\\r\\n- **`list_cluster_claims`** *(read)* - every cluster's ClusterClaims (id, platform, region, version).\\r\\n- **`get_cluster_info`** *(read)* - extended inventory from the hub ("]
[0.000, "o", "OpenShift version, nodes, console URL); needs no spoke access.\\r\\n  - `cluster` (string) - managed cluster name.\\r\\n</details>\\r\\n\\r\\n<details>\\r\\n<summary><b>observability</b> - why a cluster is unhealthy</summary>\\r\\n\\r\\n- **`get_cluster_health`** *(read)* - hub conditions, unhealthy pods, degraded deploy\"]\r\n../demo/connect-codex.cast:72:[0.000, \"o\", \" why</summary>\\r\\n\\r\\n- **`list_placements`** *(read)* - Placements and how many clusters each selects.\\r\\n  - `namespace` (string, optional) - limit to one namespace.\\r\\n- **`get_placement_decision`** *(read)* - the clusters a Placement actually selected.\\r\\n  - `placement` (string) - Placement name.\\r\\n  - `namespace` (string) - the Placement's namespace.\\r\\n- **`list_addon_placement_scores`** *(read)* - custom scores prioritizers consume.\\r\\n  - `cluster` (string) - managed cluster name.\\r\\n</details>\\r\\n\\r\\n<details>\\r\\n<summary><b>work</b> - what the hub is delivering, and the gated deploy flow</summary>\\r\\n\\r\\n- **`list_manifestworks`** *(read)* - Manife"]
[0.000, "o", "stWorks targeting a cluster.\\r\\n  - `cluster` (string) - managed cluster name.\\r\\n- **`get_manifestwork`** *(read)* - detailed status + per-resource status feedback (the \\\"why not Applied\\\").\\r\\n  - `cluster` (string), `name` (string) - target.\\r\\n- **`list_manifestworkreplicasets`** *(read)* - a template fanned across a Placement, with rollout summary.\\r\\n  - `namespace` (string, optional) - \"]\r\n../demo/connect-codex.cast:82:[0.000, \"o\", \"\\u001b[0;90m$ codex -p \\\"Explain the placement named demo-all in namespace default: which clusters does it currently sele...\\\"\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\"]\r\n../demo/connect-codex.cast:101:[0.000, \"o\", \"session id: 01a04f21-e1ab-7c30-89b1-f2ef83d12559\\r\\n--------\\r\\nuser\\r\\nExplain the placement named demo-all in namespace default: which clusters does it currently select, and why those? Keep it to a few lines.\"]\r\n../demo/connect-codex.cast:117:[4.018, \"o\", \"exec\\r\\n/bin/zsh -lc 'kubectl get placement demo-all -n default -o yaml' in /Users/sandeepbazar/01.Projects/SandeepBazar/ocm-mcp-serv"]
[0.000, "o", "er/.demo-connect\\r\\n\"]\r\n../wiki/Tools-and-Prompts.md:20:| **placement** | Placements, PlacementDecisions, AddOnPlacementScores | 3 | - |\r\n../wiki/Tools-and-Prompts.md:82:- **`cordon`** - add a `NoSelect` taint so Placements stop scheduling to the cluster.\r\n../wiki/Tools-and-Prompts.md:117:| **`why_not_scheduled`** | `cluster`, `placement`, `namespace` | explain a Placement decision from the live objects. |\r\n../wiki/Implementation.md:77:one interface - but only types on a fixed allow-list (ManagedCluster, Placement,\r\n../demo/connect-claude.cast:20:[0.647, \"o\", \"\\r\\n\\u001b[1;36m# 3b. fixtures: a cluster-set binding, a Placement, and the target namespace\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\"]\r\n../demo/connect-claude.cast:21:[0.002, \"o\", \"  placement demo-all + namespace shop ready\\r\\n\"]\r\n../demo/connect-claude.cast:28:[0.000, \"o\", \"\\u001b[0;90m$ claude -p \\\"Explain the placement named demo-all in namespace default: which clusters does it currently sele...\\\"\\u001b[0m\\r\\n\"]\r\n../demo/connect-claude.cast:29:[22.408, \"o\", \"**`demo-all` curr"]
[0.000, "o", "ently selects `cluster1`, `cluster2`, `cluster3` — the whole fleet.**\\r\\n\\r\\nWhy: it binds the `global` ClusterSet (bound in `default` via the `global` ManagedClusterSetBinding), sets no `numberOfClusters` cap, and carries no label/claim predicates — so every accepted, joined cluster in `global` qualifies. All three are `Available=True`, giving 3/3. Status confirms it: `PlacementMisconfigured=False`, `PlacementSatisfied=True`.\\r\\n\\r\\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\\r\\n- The clusters' own label says `clusterset: default`, yet they land in `global` — `global` is OCM's built-in *LabelSelector*-type ClusterSet with an empty selector, so it always contains every ManagedCluster regardless of the per-cluster clusterset label. Binding `global` is the canonical \\\"select the whole fleet\\\" idiom.\\r\\n- The binding is what makes this legal: a Placement can only draw from ClusterSets bound into *its own* namespace. Withou\"]\r"]
[0.000, "o", "\r\n../demo/connect-claude.cast:30:[0.000, \"o\", \"t the `global` binding in `default`, this same Placement would report `PlacementMisconfigured=True` and select zero clusters — a common cause of \\\"my placement matches nothing.\\\"\\r\\n- Note the two-tool split in this MCP server: `list_placements` shows *intent* (spec + conditions), `get_placement_decision` reads the *outcome* from PlacementDecisions. Intent can be satisfiable while decisions lag, so an operator diagnosing drift should always read both.\\r\\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\\r\\n\"]\r\n../demo/connect-claude.cast:65:[105.275, \"o\", \"Read the trail plus the surviving proposal record and the guardrail code that produced the refusals. Here's the log.\\r\\n\\r\\n## Operations log — 2026-08-30, 01:29:47–01:33:03 local\\r\\n\\r\\n18 audit entries, `seq` 1–18, five separate client processes, one hub (`.demo-connect`).\\r\\n\\r\\n**Fleet review** (seq 1"]
[0.000, "o", "–3, 01:29:47)\\r\\n- `get_addon_health`, `list_clusters`, `list_cluster_management_addons` — all `ok`\\r\\n- Read-only inventory sweep; no scoping args, whole fleet\\r\\n\\r\\n**Placement check** (seq 4–7, 01:30:11)\\r\\n- `get_placement_decision` on `demo-all` / `default`, then `list_placements`, `list_cluster_set_bindings`, `list_clusters`\\r\\n- Verified which clusters `demo-all` actually selects, and that the binding backing it exists — before targeting anything\\r\\n\\r\\n**Refused shortcut** (seq 9, 01:30:49)\\r\\n- `propose_manifestwork` — `storefront` → `cluster2`: 1 replica, `nginx:latest`, `securityContext.privileged: true`\\r\\n- Stated intent in the summary: *\\\"Requested for a fast ship of a new storefront\\\"*\\r\\n- Outcome `rejected` \"]\r\n../wiki/Roadmap.md:18:    long --> l2[Placement-aware fleet actions]\r\n../wiki/Roadmap.md:53:- **Placement-aware fleet actions**: proposals that target a scored subset of\r\n../wiki/The-Idea.md:12:| `Placement` | scheduling: which clusters match a rule | how humans target sub"]
