[0.000, "o", "ator reports: {symptom}\\n\\n\"\r\nocm/lib/python3.14/site-packages/ocm_mcp_server/server.py-917-        \"Follow the safe remediation workflow:\\n\"\r\nocm/lib/python3.14/site-packages/ocm_mcp_server/server.py-918-        \"1. Investigate with the read tools (list_clusters, get_cluster_health, query_events, \"\r\nocm/lib/python3.14/site-packages/ocm_mcp_server/server.py-919-        \"get_pod_logs, get_manifestwork) until you can name the root cause with evidence.\\n\"\r\nocm/lib/python3.14/site-packages/ocm_mcp_server/server.py-920-        \"2. Decide the smallest change that fixes it. For a workload change, call \"\r\nocm/lib/python3.14/site-packages/ocm_mcp_server/server.py:921:        \"propose_manifestwork with pinned images and a precise summary. For a cluster \"\r\nocm/lib/python3.14/site-packages/ocm_mcp_server/server.py-922-        \"lifecycle change (cordon, uncordon, set a label, accept a cluster), call \"\r\nocm/lib/python3.14/site-packages/ocm_mcp_server/server.py-923-        \"propose_cluster_action.\\n\"\r\nocm/lib/python3.14/sit"]
[0.000, "o", "e-packages/ocm_mcp_server/server.py-924-        \"3. If the proposal is REJECTED by static guardrails or Kyverno, read the reason, \"\r\nocm/lib/python3.14/site-packages/ocm_mcp_server/server.py-925-        \"correct the manifest, and propose again. Never try to bypass a rejection.\\n\"\r\nocm/lib/python3.14/site-packages/ocm_mcp_server/server.py-926-        \"4. Tell the operator the proposal id and ask them to run `ocm-mcp approve <id>` and \"\r\nocm/lib/python3.14/site-packages/ocm_mcp_server/server.py-927-        \"give you the token. Wait for it.\\n\"\r\nocm/lib/python3.14/site-packages/ocm_mcp_server/server.py-928-        \"5. Call the matching apply tool with the token. Then verify recovery with reads.\\n\"\r\nocm/lib/python3.14/site-packages/ocm_mcp_server/server.py-929-        \"6. Finish by calling get_audit_trail and writing an accurate incident summary.\"\r\n\r\n"]
