[0.000, "o", "b8a57a5cb94fe7df0bf6b71658577fe1bd9\"}\r\n{\"tool\": \"propose_manifestwork\", \"args\": {\"cluster\": \"cluster1\", \"name\": \"payments-command-fix\", \"summary\": \"payments Deployment (shop namespace, cluster1) is CrashLoopBackOff right now: pod logs show \\\"/bin/sh: can't open 'netexec': No such file or directory\\\" \\u2014 the container's command overrides the agnhost image's entrypoint incorrectly (invoking sh with 'netexec' as a script path instead of passing it as an arg). cluster3's payments Deployment runs the identical agnhost:2.47 image successfully with command=[\\\"/agnhost\\\"], args=[\\\"netexec\\\",\\\"--http-port=8080\\\",\\\"--udp-port=8081\\\"] (confirmed healthy via live logs: \\\"Started HTTP server on port 8080\\\"). This patch sets the container \\\"payments\\\" command/args on cluster1 to match that proven-working cluster3 pattern exactly. It does not touch replicas, selector, env, or any other field. Pod-security fields are declared to satisfy this hub's Kyverno guardrails, matching the pattern already validated in prior pending"]
