[0.000, "o", "ated\r\r\n- seq 14, 01:32:38: `apply_manifestwork` with approval token (redacted in the audit record) → `ok`, 36 ms\r\r\n- Proposal record: `status: applied`, `approved_by: sandeepbazar`, `applied_uid 1abb72de-…`\r\r\n- Token was single-use — `used_tokens.jsonl` shows `jti aeb3c170…` burned at `used_at 1788033758`, ~1h before its `exp`\r\r\n\r\r\n**Verification** (seq 15–18, 01:32:42–01:33:03)\r\r\n\r\r\n- `get_manifestwork` cluster2/storefront → `ok`\r\r\n- `get_cluster_health` cluster2, twice (01:32:47, 01:32:53) → `ok`\r\r\n- `query_events` cluster2 / `shop`, limit 40 → `ok`\r\r\n\r\r\n**Chain integrity**\r\r\n- `seq` 1–18 unbroken, `prev` on each entry matches the predecessor's `hash` at every link; seq 1 has empty `prev` as expected\r\r\n- One mutating call total (seq 14); every other entry is a read or a proposal\r\r\n\r\r\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\r\r\n- `classify_outcome` (`tracing.py:302`) is the reason this trail is readable as"]
[0.000, "o", " evidence: tools **return normally** when they refuse, so a naive wrapper would log the privileged-nginx attempt as `ok`. Parsing the `REJECTED`/`FAILED`/`ERROR` prefix out of the return string is what keeps seq 9 and 11 from becoming false successes — and the docstring says explicitly that the eval harness scores from this log.\r\r\n- The two rejections are more valuable than the approval. They show the \r\ngate is *static* — refusing before a human is ever asked — so the operator's attention is only spent on proposals that already pass the floor. `server.py:972` bakes this in, instructing reports to cite rejected proposals \"as evidence the guardrails held.\"\r\r\n- The second refusal is the interesting one: the agent produced a genuinely hardened spec and was still blocked on one omission. That's a deny-by-default policy rather than a heuristic — `automountServiceAccountToken` must be *explicitly* `false`, since an absent field and a deliberate `false` are indistinguishable to a reviewer skimming YAML.\r\r\n`"]
[0.000, "o", "─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\r\r\n\r\r\n"]
