[0.000, "o", "nd no dependencies. It runs in CI too, so a\\r\\n../README.md:661:closed (expired token, replayed token, apply-scoped token refused for rollback, read-only\\r\\n../examples/README.md:29:\\\"\"]\r\r\n6126:1018:[0.000, \"o\", \"s applied 4 days ago.</p>\\r\\n../.bob/artifacts/the-operator-s-chair-medium-paste.html:172:  <p>Before I started using the agent, my maintenance workflow was: update a label, update a placement, wait, verify. Now it is: ask the agent to propose a cordon, approve it with <code>ocm-mcp approve</code>, verify the Placement excluded the cluster, do the maintenance, then propose and approve the uncordon. Each step has a record. The audit log entry for the cordon includes my process identity and the stated reason. \r\n6127:When someone asks \\\"why was Frankfurt out of rotation for four days,\\\" the answer is one <code>get-audit-trail</code> call away.</p>\\r\\n../.bob/artifacts/the-operator-s-chair-medium-paste.html:210:  <p>The full <a href=\\\"https://github.com/sandeepbazar/ocm-mcp-server/tree/main/demo\\\">demo</"]
